WEBVTT

00:00:07.110 --> 00:00:11.440
AUGUST 6, 2095 - NINE SCHOOLS COMPETITION DAY FOUR

00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:11.820
All right! To celebrate
Shizuku's victory in Speed Shooting...

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:13.620
and the strong finishes
by Kazumi and myself,

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:17.290
and Honoka making past
the qualifying round in Battle Board...

00:00:17.290 --> 00:00:19.370
Cheers!

00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:25.460
Thank goodness Day One of the
Rookie Events ended without a hitch!

00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:29.380
I'm off tomorrow,
but you all have matches, right?

00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:33.260
Shizuku, Eimi and I
will be taking part in Ice Pillars Break.

00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:35.680
Nanami and I are in Cloudball.

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:38.980
Isn't Isshiki of Third High in Cloudball, too?

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:41.390
Yeah. You can't let
your guard down against her.

00:00:41.390 --> 00:00:43.560
No need to worry, guys.

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:45.150
Since I'm competing,

00:00:45.150 --> 00:00:48.740
I can guarantee you
a flamboyant victory for First High!

00:00:51.030 --> 00:00:54.160
Is this your first time seeing Subaru do that?

00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:57.160
Because of her hereditary
Awareness Block skill,

00:00:57.160 --> 00:01:01.500
she tends to speak and act in a way
that will leave a lasting impression.

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:03.790
I-Is that right?

00:01:03.790 --> 00:01:06.590
I wish I was competing
in Pillars Break, too.

00:01:06.590 --> 00:01:09.420
Tatsuya's your engineer, right?

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:11.800
That's right. You can trust him.

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:15.800
Wasn't your Active Air Mine
a spell created by Tatsuya, too?

00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:17.680
So's my Flash!

00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:22.940
Really, that, too? Man, I wish he could've
been the engineer for Cloudball, too!

00:01:22.940 --> 00:01:25.520
Since my brother only has one body,

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:28.190
he can't possibly work
on two events at the same time.

00:01:28.190 --> 00:01:30.860
But I know where Nanami's coming from.

00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:34.860
As of now, he's undefeated
in every event he's worked on.

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:37.280
That's a feat that would entitle
anyone to swagger more.

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:42.500
But I hear that he declined to have
his name recorded in the Index, too.

00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:46.080
Yes. That's a bad habit of my brother's.

00:01:48.590 --> 00:01:50.380
Please tell me.

00:01:50.380 --> 00:01:54.380
Did you decline
to be named in the Index?

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:57.600
Did our aunt and her intentions
have anything to do with that?

00:01:57.600 --> 00:01:59.260
That's right.

00:01:59.260 --> 00:02:00.810
I knew it.

00:02:00.810 --> 00:02:03.230
So, that's the reason.

00:02:03.230 --> 00:02:06.610
The shackles that bind you, Brother,
are the Yotsubas' existence.

00:02:06.610 --> 00:02:09.230
My existence.

00:02:09.230 --> 00:02:13.780
If only I had more power...

00:02:13.780 --> 00:02:16.820
Miyuki...

00:02:16.820 --> 00:02:21.120
You don't have to worry about those things.

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:23.040
Brother...

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:26.710
Even if the world
becomes your enemy,

00:02:26.710 --> 00:02:30.210
I will always be on your side.

00:02:30.210 --> 00:02:32.130
Please don't ever forget that!

00:04:08.140 --> 00:04:12.350
AUGUST 7, 2095

00:04:08.520 --> 00:04:12.650
Was Third High's Airi Isshiki
really that powerful?

00:04:12.650 --> 00:04:15.820
That speed of hers was superhuman!

00:04:15.820 --> 00:04:20.490
And I dialed it up to the human
threshold limit during virtual training!

00:04:20.490 --> 00:04:23.580
Even if that's true...

00:04:23.580 --> 00:04:26.870
Ms. Isshiki will slow down for sure.

00:04:26.870 --> 00:04:30.290
So long as I have my special skill.

00:04:33.750 --> 00:04:36.050
The Rookie Events continue to heat up!

00:04:36.050 --> 00:04:39.220
Already, the Women's Cloudball final is upon us!

00:04:42.090 --> 00:04:45.180
Going up against
First High School's Subaru Satomi...

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:48.600
is Third High School's Airi Isshiki!

00:04:51.430 --> 00:04:53.890
"AUGUST 7 ROOKIE EVENT"
"SUBARU SATOMI (FIRST HIGH SCHOOL)"
"AIRI ISSHIKI (THIRD HIGH SCHOOL)"

00:04:55.570 --> 00:04:56.780
In this event...

00:04:56.780 --> 00:05:01.110
the players will vie to deposit the most balls
in their opponent's court within the time limit!

00:05:01.110 --> 00:05:05.530
And the balls are flying all over the court
so fast, you can barely see them!

00:05:04.720 --> 00:05:06.700
SUBARU SATOMI

00:05:04.720 --> 00:05:06.700
AIRI ISSHIKI

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:09.540
Something's wrong.

00:05:09.540 --> 00:05:13.000
I know that I'm aiming
for wherever she's not standing.

00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:17.920
An illusion?
No, she's actually there.

00:05:17.920 --> 00:05:21.340
And yet, I can't sense her presence at all.

00:05:21.340 --> 00:05:23.680
My Awareness Block skill
is a type of BS Magic

00:05:23.680 --> 00:05:27.930
that allows me to conceal my presence
even when I'm visible.

00:05:27.930 --> 00:05:32.230
Even if you do spot me,
there's nothing you can do.

00:05:32.230 --> 00:05:35.860
She must've cast
some kind of unique spell...

00:05:35.860 --> 00:05:38.650
but there's no time to ponder the reason.

00:05:38.650 --> 00:05:40.190
In that case...

00:05:44.070 --> 00:05:46.200
I won't watch for her movements.

00:05:46.200 --> 00:05:48.330
I'll just focus on the balls.

00:05:48.330 --> 00:05:50.290
Pick up the pace...

00:05:50.290 --> 00:05:53.120
and return every single ball that I can see!

00:05:58.960 --> 00:06:00.300
Was that a fluke?

00:06:00.300 --> 00:06:01.800
No...

00:06:04.380 --> 00:06:08.680
She's clearly accelerating!

00:06:08.680 --> 00:06:11.310
I-I can't possibly reach them all!

00:06:11.310 --> 00:06:15.190
If it's a test of pure speed,
no one has a chance against me.

00:06:15.190 --> 00:06:16.810
Because I'm Éclair...

00:06:16.810 --> 00:06:18.060
Lightning!

00:06:19.190 --> 00:06:21.150
Match over!

00:06:21.150 --> 00:06:23.240
Winner of the Women's
Cloudball Rookie Event...

00:06:23.240 --> 00:06:27.570
Airi Isshiki of Third High School!

00:06:30.950 --> 00:06:32.870
Subaru...

00:06:32.870 --> 00:06:34.870
That was tough, huh?

00:06:34.870 --> 00:06:37.210
Wow, that's our Airi, all right!

00:06:37.210 --> 00:06:39.290
Huh?

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:46.130
Hey, you're that Light Magic wielder
from yesterday! Fancy meeting you here!

00:06:46.130 --> 00:06:48.180
Uh, I guess.

00:06:48.180 --> 00:06:50.970
Is the runner-up a friend of yours?

00:06:50.970 --> 00:06:52.560
She may have gotten tripled up by Airi,

00:06:52.560 --> 00:06:56.850
but getting a double-digit score off Airi
is nothing to sneeze at!

00:06:56.850 --> 00:07:00.190
But the fact that she got
such a huge lead...

00:07:00.190 --> 00:07:03.360
I wonder if it has something to do
with the light at her neck.

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:07.360
Ah... You were able to see that light, yes?

00:07:08.030 --> 00:07:12.580
If you could see that,
you must be hypersensitive to light.

00:07:12.580 --> 00:07:15.830
Now I understand how your Flash Spell
yesterday could be so precise.

00:07:16.670 --> 00:07:21.500
What you saw was the light
from Airi's necklace CAD.

00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:24.510
Since it only contains
the bare minimum of magic,

00:07:24.510 --> 00:07:28.970
the amount of light is minute,
so I'm impressed you could see it.

00:07:28.970 --> 00:07:34.270
Airi's magic consists of a spell to directly
recognize perceived information with her mind,

00:07:34.270 --> 00:07:39.150
and a spell to directly command
the body to return shots, run,

00:07:39.150 --> 00:07:42.860
and control her CAD, all with her mind.

00:07:42.860 --> 00:07:47.950
Y-You mean her body starts moving
before she can even think?

00:07:47.950 --> 00:07:51.160
Well, before she can see, to be precise.

00:07:51.160 --> 00:07:54.240
That's why Airi's known as Éclair.

00:07:54.240 --> 00:07:56.160
That kind of magic actually exists?

00:07:56.160 --> 00:07:59.710
But that's such crucial information.
Are you sure it's okay to share it with me?

00:07:59.710 --> 00:08:01.500
When I'm with a rival team?

00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:02.710
Not a problem!

00:08:02.710 --> 00:08:07.050
As powerful as Airi is, it wouldn't slow her
down even if her opponents were to find out!

00:08:08.550 --> 00:08:13.600
From the looks of it, you're here to watch
the Ice Pillars Break matches alone, right?

00:08:13.600 --> 00:08:16.770
How about watching with me?

00:08:18.600 --> 00:08:21.310
I let myself cave in to her.

00:08:21.310 --> 00:08:24.020
I really am a pushover!

00:08:24.020 --> 00:08:25.730
I've got to be more careful.

00:08:25.730 --> 00:08:27.320
You got that right!

00:08:27.320 --> 00:08:30.450
Being as you're a little fragile!

00:08:30.450 --> 00:08:32.160
Did I just say that out loud?

00:08:32.160 --> 00:08:33.870
Hey, the match is about to start!

00:08:34.950 --> 00:08:39.290
In Ice Pillars Break, the players try
to destroy their opponent's ice pillars

00:08:39.290 --> 00:08:42.880
while defending their own twelve pillars!

00:08:42.880 --> 00:08:46.550
And their costumes are also riveting!

00:08:46.550 --> 00:08:49.470
So, Shiori went with her
fencing outfit, huh?

00:08:51.590 --> 00:08:53.260
I like that look in her eye.

00:09:05.320 --> 00:09:07.940
If I can boost
the data fortification output...

00:09:07.940 --> 00:09:10.400
I can prevent the ice from breaking!

00:09:10.400 --> 00:09:14.280
Futile.

00:09:14.280 --> 00:09:15.870
No way!

00:09:15.870 --> 00:09:18.910
The ice was fortified.
How can it break so easily?

00:09:18.910 --> 00:09:22.420
That magic can't be blocked
by a counterattack like that.

00:09:22.420 --> 00:09:25.460
Since Shiori's magic starts in midair,

00:09:25.460 --> 00:09:29.420
you can't stop the spell from activating
by fortifying the ice's data.

00:09:29.420 --> 00:09:33.130
Not only that, but since
she's generating multiple oscillation waves,

00:09:33.130 --> 00:09:35.010
they intersect at the synthesis point...

00:09:35.010 --> 00:09:37.850
and become many times stronger!

00:09:39.890 --> 00:09:41.520
Since it's come to this...

00:09:44.100 --> 00:09:47.190
Now the oscillation waves can't get hit
when they synthesize.

00:09:47.190 --> 00:09:48.480
How's that?

00:09:50.740 --> 00:09:52.030
Just as I thought.

00:09:52.030 --> 00:09:56.700
You disabled your data fortification spell
to move those ice pillars.

00:09:56.700 --> 00:10:01.000
There's no need to unleash layers
of oscillation on such fragile ice.

00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:02.660
You're finished!

00:10:06.410 --> 00:10:08.370
"THIRD HIGH SCHOOL"

00:10:11.550 --> 00:10:15.300
Shiori's back in full force!

00:10:15.300 --> 00:10:17.970
She has such an intense look on her face.

00:10:17.970 --> 00:10:19.430
I should, too!

00:10:20.640 --> 00:10:25.390
"EIMI AKECHI (FIRST HIGH SCHOOL)"
"ANJU SHINOZAKI (EIGHTH HIGH SCHOOL)"

00:10:21.430 --> 00:10:25.940
Next up, Eimi Akechi of First High School!

00:10:25.940 --> 00:10:28.270
Huh! That's your friend, isn't it?

00:10:28.270 --> 00:10:30.570
Yay! Thanks for waiting!

00:10:30.570 --> 00:10:34.110
I'm going to smash your hearts!

00:10:34.110 --> 00:10:35.910
Bam!

00:10:42.660 --> 00:10:47.330
Eimi, your specialty
is moving buildings, right?

00:10:42.740 --> 00:10:47.080
JULY 21, 2095 - FIRST HIGH SCHOOL

00:10:47.330 --> 00:10:52.550
Yep! I can handle the really big ones, too!
And my activation speed is second to none!

00:10:52.550 --> 00:11:00.140
I see. Then, can you move a pillar from Ice
Pillars Break as if it were a single building?

00:11:00.140 --> 00:11:01.560
You bet I can!

00:11:01.560 --> 00:11:03.730
Not to brag, but when I was a kid,

00:11:03.730 --> 00:11:07.850
I used to move around
the stone pillars in my yard for fun!

00:11:07.850 --> 00:11:10.270
The ones like you see in Stonehenge.

00:11:10.270 --> 00:11:11.980
Well, that's...

00:11:11.980 --> 00:11:14.440
sure impressive.
In more than one sense of the word.

00:11:14.440 --> 00:11:18.030
Well, but I did get an earful
from my grandma.

00:11:18.030 --> 00:11:21.120
That kind of experience
definitely works in our favor.

00:11:21.120 --> 00:11:24.500
Let me come up with a spell
with that in mind.

00:11:26.080 --> 00:11:29.040
So fast! And this magic sequence...

00:11:29.040 --> 00:11:32.960
is totally simple and so streamlined!

00:11:32.960 --> 00:11:35.220
Now I'm sure I've got this!

00:11:35.590 --> 00:11:38.420
AUGUST 7, 2095 - ICE PILLARS BREAK WOMEN'S ROOKIE EVENT QUALIFYING ROUNDS

00:11:38.840 --> 00:11:40.050
All right.

00:11:40.050 --> 00:11:41.550
Let's get started!

00:11:43.470 --> 00:11:45.600
Yippee ki yay!

00:11:47.140 --> 00:11:48.350
Ah!

00:11:48.350 --> 00:11:53.480
What's going on, Ms. Akechi?
You just toppled your own pillar!

00:11:53.480 --> 00:11:56.190
Let's go!

00:11:58.200 --> 00:11:59.280
Huh?

00:12:04.660 --> 00:12:06.250
Who in their right mind...

00:12:06.250 --> 00:12:09.540
She sacrificed one of her own pillars
to go after her opponent's?

00:12:09.540 --> 00:12:11.080
That's our Eimi!

00:12:14.710 --> 00:12:19.880
Winner, Eimi Akechi of First High School!

00:12:19.880 --> 00:12:22.390
I feel awesome!

00:12:23.660 --> 00:12:27.850
FIRST HIGH SCHOOL

00:12:25.390 --> 00:12:28.060
Good job, Shizuku, Eimi.

00:12:28.060 --> 00:12:30.560
The crowd sure had a blast, too!

00:12:31.770 --> 00:12:33.650
I'm so glad I was able to win.

00:12:33.650 --> 00:12:37.400
Although those two
are looking depressed...

00:12:37.400 --> 00:12:38.700
I can't believe it.

00:12:38.700 --> 00:12:41.160
Isshiki was so powerful.

00:12:41.160 --> 00:12:45.290
Come on, cheer up!
You both achieved a lot, you know!

00:12:45.290 --> 00:12:47.950
You were the runner-up, Subaru...

00:12:47.950 --> 00:12:51.460
and you came in a respectable 6th, Nanami!

00:12:51.460 --> 00:12:55.250
For both of you to finish so high
at the same time is still a feat.

00:12:55.250 --> 00:12:58.380
It's a huge victory, right on the heels
of the Speed Shooting Event!

00:12:58.380 --> 00:13:01.590
Ms. Saegusa and the others
were really thrilled, too!

00:13:06.310 --> 00:13:08.600
Well, I guess
it's not too shabby a result, huh?

00:13:08.600 --> 00:13:14.270
Right! If only I hadn't drawn Isshiki,
I might've cracked the podium, too!

00:13:14.270 --> 00:13:16.150
Well, now they're all hyper again.

00:13:16.150 --> 00:13:18.360
But it's all good, don't you think?

00:13:18.360 --> 00:13:21.280
Still, I can't believe your energy, Eimi!

00:13:21.280 --> 00:13:25.240
After playing cards until dawn
yesterday and the day before!

00:13:25.240 --> 00:13:26.990
Huh? You were?

00:13:26.990 --> 00:13:30.370
Well, since Eimi's the type
who whoops it up until she's totally spent.

00:13:30.370 --> 00:13:32.670
F-For the love of all that's holy,
let us sleep now.

00:13:32.670 --> 00:13:35.790
Tomorrow... I mean
today we have matches.

00:13:35.790 --> 00:13:38.340
Not yet, not yet! One more game!

00:13:38.340 --> 00:13:41.590
You should be ashamed!
We're not playing with you anymore, okay?

00:13:41.590 --> 00:13:43.640
It's your turn next, right, Miyuki?

00:13:43.640 --> 00:13:44.970
Yes.

00:13:44.970 --> 00:13:50.640
This is your first match of the tournament,
so I'm really looking forward to it.

00:13:50.640 --> 00:13:52.140
Are you?

00:13:52.140 --> 00:13:55.980
Then I'll have to do my best,
so as not to disappoint you.

00:13:57.730 --> 00:14:00.360
Come to think of it,
for the Ice Pillars Break Event...

00:14:00.360 --> 00:14:02.030
if everyone keeps winning,

00:14:02.030 --> 00:14:06.910
then Shizuku and Eimi will have to go up
against Miyuki eventually.

00:14:06.910 --> 00:14:11.000
Who should I root for if that happens?

00:14:11.000 --> 00:14:13.620
Hey, what kind of costume
are you wearing, Miyuki?

00:14:13.620 --> 00:14:16.630
Both Shizuku and Eimi
really went all out, remember?

00:14:16.630 --> 00:14:19.000
My outfit is quite orthodox.

00:14:19.000 --> 00:14:21.420
As for what it is,
you'll see soon enough!

00:14:24.970 --> 00:14:27.300
That player will be up next.

00:14:27.300 --> 00:14:30.390
Well, Airi's had her eye
on her from the start.

00:14:30.390 --> 00:14:31.770
Can't wait to see her!

00:14:31.770 --> 00:14:33.230
Yes.

00:14:33.230 --> 00:14:34.690
Let me see the talent

00:14:34.690 --> 00:14:40.480
that earned you a spot among the upperclassmen
in the official Mirage Bat Event, just like me.

00:14:40.480 --> 00:14:43.900
These are the qualifying rounds
for the Women's Ice Pillars Break Rookie Event!

00:14:43.900 --> 00:14:46.820
And now, here's Ms. Miyuki Shiba,
taking the field!

00:14:46.820 --> 00:14:50.620
All right! What kind of outfit
will Miyuki be wearing--

00:15:02.090 --> 00:15:05.300
She looks amazing in that kimono!

00:15:05.300 --> 00:15:06.300
Gorgeous!

00:15:06.300 --> 00:15:07.720
That looks so good on her!

00:15:07.720 --> 00:15:09.680
Orthodox?

00:15:12.020 --> 00:15:17.020
Oh, poor thing.
Her opponent is totally paralyzed.

00:15:17.020 --> 00:15:20.270
Is Miyuki's outfit part of her strategy?

00:15:20.270 --> 00:15:22.730
Leave it to you to see it that way.

00:15:22.730 --> 00:15:25.280
It's not an especially unusual outfit.

00:15:25.280 --> 00:15:30.030
It's a standard magical costume
that's been used in Japan since ancient times.

00:15:30.030 --> 00:15:32.870
Somehow he's just a bit off, this kid.

00:15:32.870 --> 00:15:34.330
Yep.

00:15:35.960 --> 00:15:39.080
First of all, I must calm myself.

00:15:39.080 --> 00:15:43.760
Merely thinking can cause my magic
to interfere with phenomena.

00:15:43.760 --> 00:15:48.050
If I were to jump the gun,
I'd cause trouble for my brother, my engineer...

00:15:48.050 --> 00:15:49.840
That would be unthinkable.

00:16:05.900 --> 00:16:07.070
What the...

00:16:07.070 --> 00:16:08.740
Wh-What is this?

00:16:08.740 --> 00:16:11.030
D-Don't tell me this spell is...

00:16:11.030 --> 00:16:14.200
Midrange Area Oscillation Magic.

00:16:14.200 --> 00:16:15.830
Inferno!

00:16:16.580 --> 00:16:19.040
What? You mean that advanced magic?

00:16:19.040 --> 00:16:20.380
No way.

00:16:20.380 --> 00:16:23.590
Burning her opponent's ice
with blazing hellfire...

00:16:23.590 --> 00:16:27.550
Meanwhile, she's protecting her own ice
completely with an ultralow temperature lid.

00:16:27.550 --> 00:16:31.260
Who knew there was a
high school student capable of this feat?

00:16:32.550 --> 00:16:35.970
Who are you, Miyuki Shiba?

00:16:42.650 --> 00:16:43.940
And that's the match!

00:16:43.940 --> 00:16:47.990
Winner, Miyuki Shiba of First High School!

00:16:49.530 --> 00:16:51.030
Miyuki sure was amazing!

00:16:51.030 --> 00:16:53.280
Who knew she was this amazing?

00:16:57.410 --> 00:17:01.080
Oh man! Now that was a sight to see!

00:17:01.080 --> 00:17:02.420
Let's go for some tea!

00:17:02.420 --> 00:17:04.630
You sure are laid-back, Toko.

00:17:05.710 --> 00:17:08.300
You two are so lucky.

00:17:08.300 --> 00:17:11.340
Since you might get
the chance to take her on.

00:17:11.340 --> 00:17:12.840
Do you want to take her on?

00:17:12.840 --> 00:17:14.550
Well, why wouldn't I?

00:17:14.550 --> 00:17:16.470
It's a chance to go head-to-head

00:17:16.470 --> 00:17:20.600
in a no-holds-barred environment
against a magician of that caliber!

00:17:20.600 --> 00:17:22.650
Probably a once-in-a-lifetime chance!

00:17:22.650 --> 00:17:24.480
You're right.

00:17:24.480 --> 00:17:29.570
It's true that Miyuki Shiba
is a player of immense magical power.

00:17:29.570 --> 00:17:34.910
That's why triumphing over her
will be especially meaningful.

00:17:34.910 --> 00:17:40.040
As long as it's not a mere test of magical
power, but an event that goes by the book...

00:17:40.040 --> 00:17:43.330
you can defeat any magician
no matter how powerful.

00:17:45.170 --> 00:17:48.880
And I've logged so many hours
of training to accomplish that. So...

00:17:48.880 --> 00:17:51.420
we can win for sure!

00:17:53.010 --> 00:17:54.340
Absolutely!

00:17:54.340 --> 00:17:56.260
You said it!

00:18:01.180 --> 00:18:03.350
I knew all about it...

00:18:03.350 --> 00:18:05.860
but how powerful is Miyuki?

00:18:05.860 --> 00:18:10.320
Just thinking that I might have to face off
with her gives me a stomachache!

00:18:10.320 --> 00:18:12.200
Hey...

00:18:12.200 --> 00:18:16.490
That's not like you
to look so worried, Eimi.

00:18:16.490 --> 00:18:20.000
Even I can get freaked out
once in a while, you know!

00:18:20.000 --> 00:18:24.000
I don't blame you. After all,
your next opponent is pretty formidable!

00:18:24.000 --> 00:18:25.540
Huh?

00:18:25.540 --> 00:18:31.130
Remember? It's Ms. Kanou of Third High,
who also competed in Speed Shooting, too.

00:18:31.130 --> 00:18:35.800
I watched her match, but she pulverized
her opponent's pillars just like that!

00:18:35.800 --> 00:18:37.260
Oh!

00:18:37.260 --> 00:18:42.390
Darn it! This is no time
to be worrying about taking on Miyuki!

00:18:42.390 --> 00:18:44.940
Wh-What am I going to do?

00:18:55.030 --> 00:18:57.030
Thank you, Tatsuya!

00:18:57.030 --> 00:18:59.870
Thanks to you,
I somehow made it into the Top 10!

00:18:59.870 --> 00:19:02.450
Miyuki!

00:19:02.450 --> 00:19:05.750
Your Inferno was mind-blowing!

00:19:05.750 --> 00:19:07.960
Is that thanks to Tatsuya, too?

00:19:07.960 --> 00:19:12.880
Yes, of course. That spell could never
have been unleashed without my brother.

00:19:12.880 --> 00:19:16.050
Huh? That's what I thought,
but it's true!

00:19:16.050 --> 00:19:18.090
Amazing!

00:19:18.090 --> 00:19:23.140
Thank goodness. Now everyone
acknowledges my brother's abilities.

00:19:23.140 --> 00:19:26.020
The first year women's table
sure looks cheery!

00:19:26.020 --> 00:19:29.150
Well, they did dominate
the podium, more or less.

00:19:29.150 --> 00:19:33.400
Especially the events
he was in charge of. Total sweep.

00:19:33.400 --> 00:19:36.110
And because they turned down
Shiba's support,

00:19:36.110 --> 00:19:39.450
the boys aren't doing too well.
Night and day, much?

00:19:39.450 --> 00:19:40.740
Oh dear.

00:19:51.750 --> 00:19:57.180
Boy, am I out of luck! One more win,
and I could've been in the final league!

00:19:57.180 --> 00:19:59.180
Are you still moping about that?

00:19:59.180 --> 00:20:02.680
You've got Tatsuya's support,
so try to be more confident!

00:20:02.680 --> 00:20:06.230
I know I should, but...

00:20:06.230 --> 00:20:11.230
just thinking about tomorrow totally kills
both my confidence and my appetite.

00:20:11.230 --> 00:20:13.230
I'm not seeing any loss of appetite.

00:20:19.780 --> 00:20:23.370
Well, well! Students of First High...
Good evening.

00:20:23.370 --> 00:20:25.290
Did you just have dinner?

00:20:25.290 --> 00:20:26.410
U-Um...

00:20:26.410 --> 00:20:27.540
Yes.

00:20:27.540 --> 00:20:30.000
We just finished now.

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:32.210
Are you on your way in?

00:20:33.800 --> 00:20:36.920
Yes. What a shame that we missed you.

00:20:36.920 --> 00:20:39.590
But I'm glad that we met now.

00:20:41.390 --> 00:20:43.100
Miyuki Shiba...

00:20:43.100 --> 00:20:47.350
Earlier, I spoke to you
in an insulting manner.

00:20:47.350 --> 00:20:52.690
But I've come to realize
that my perception was clearly wrong.

00:20:52.690 --> 00:20:55.980
I'd like to offer my sincerest
apologies for my rude behavior.

00:20:55.980 --> 00:20:59.740
You're a magician of the highest caliber
among our generation.

00:20:59.740 --> 00:21:04.660
That's precisely why I'm planning
to go all out to defeat you...

00:21:04.660 --> 00:21:09.870
and leave this Nine Schools Competition
with Third High victorious.

00:21:11.120 --> 00:21:12.460
Oh boy!

00:21:12.460 --> 00:21:14.250
There they go again this year!

00:21:14.250 --> 00:21:16.130
Hey! You're enjoying this too much!

00:21:17.710 --> 00:21:20.010
Right.

00:21:20.010 --> 00:21:25.470
Needless to say, I have no intention
of losing to you, either.

00:21:25.470 --> 00:21:28.480
Let's all give it our all, then.

00:21:36.690 --> 00:21:38.900
They're both unbelievable!

00:21:38.900 --> 00:21:41.950
Neither of them has
the thought of losing on their minds!

00:21:43.240 --> 00:21:45.280
So cool!

00:21:45.280 --> 00:21:46.910
I should be that way, too!

00:21:53.380 --> 00:21:56.630
It's not as if my defeat
is a foregone conclusion yet.

00:21:56.630 --> 00:21:59.260
I'm just going to do all that I can!

00:21:59.260 --> 00:22:00.840
That's all I can do, right?

00:22:05.760 --> 00:22:08.640
All right! Just watch me! Yippee ki--

00:22:08.640 --> 00:22:10.390
Go to sleep already!
